+# E2E Test Guide — `/sc:pr-submit` (`5.0.0`)
+
+- **Capability:** `/sc:pr-submit` opens a PR on the repository of your `origin` remote, or attaches to one with `--pr <N>`, and at `--monitor 1` to `3` (default 3) watches the Augment and Codex reviews: level 1 proposes fixes only, level 2 fixes locally and stops before pushing, level 3 fixes, pushes one commit per cycle, replies to and resolves the fixed threads and asks each reviewer to look again. It refuses a checkout that is not the PR head (`pr_head_mismatch`) and a `--max-rounds` above 5; `--yes` was removed in 5.0.0.
+- **Audience:** end user
+- **Source of truth:** `src/superclaude/commands/pr-submit.md:8,25-58,66,85`; `src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/SKILL.md:77,212-230,236-248,267-277,279-291,303-327`; `src/superclaude/pr_submit/fsm.py:30-41,76-78,111-126,528-600`; `src/superclaude/pr_submit/reviewers.py:63-70`; `src/superclaude/pr_submit/run_log.py:81-82,303-313`; `src/superclaude/pr_submit/models.py:43,61,68-82,89`; `src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/refs/detection-contract.md:29,34`, `refs/review-retrigger.md:3-7`, `refs/state-machine.md:32,45,95-104`, `refs/loop-guard.md:69-83`; `src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/scripts/poll-augment-review.sh:8,18`, `poll-ci-checks.sh:18,30`, `retrigger-review.sh:23,41`; `CHANGELOG.md:47-54,206-217,223`; `docs/releases/v5.0.0.md:234`; repository `CLAUDE.md:64,66`
+- **Est. time:** `Tier A: 3 minutes. Tier B: 5-10 minutes (clone and dependency install). Tier C: 1-3 hours, mostly waiting for the reviewers and CI (UNVERIFIED estimate: it depends on reviewer latency, the number of findings and the CI run time).`
+
+## Preconditions
+
+- IronClaude 5.0.0 installed for your user (`superclaude install` done): `superclaude --version` prints `SuperClaude, version 5.0.0`.
+- `git`, `gh`, `jq` and `uv` on your `PATH`. The poll script stops without `gh` or `jq` (`src/superclaude/skills/sc-pr-submit-protocol/scripts/poll-augment-review.sh:19-20`).
+- Tier C only: `gh auth status` shows you logged in with push rights to `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude`, your `git` commit name and email are set, and the Augment Code app and/or the Codex connector (`chatgpt-codex-connector`) are installed on `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude` (UNVERIFIED: this guide cannot check which apps are installed; with neither, the run ends `terminal_augment_no_response`). The `claude` CLI is logged in; every Tier C step uses API tokens.
+- `/tmp/d07` does not exist (`[ ! -e /tmp/d07 ] && echo OK` prints `OK`). Every local file this guide creates is under `/tmp/d07`. No step edits your real `~/.claude`. The Tier C sessions still write there in ways no step controls: Claude Code saves each session's history, and the hooks that `superclaude install` registers write state and log files under `~/.claude/state/` and `~/.claude/logs/` at session start and on each prompt (`src/superclaude/hooks/hooks.json:18,49`; `src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/freshness-session-start.sh:8-9`, `freshness-user-prompt.sh:8-10`, `auggie-flag-clear.sh:10-12`).
+- Tier C creates real state on GitHub: one sandbox branch and one PR on `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude`, plus review replies, a fix commit and re-review comments on that PR. Those steps are tagged `[EXTERNAL]`. Use only the sandbox branch this guide creates, and close the PR in Cleanup. Every PR in this guide must be on `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude`: a PR URL with any other owner (for example the public upstream parent of the fork) is a FAIL; close that PR at once (repository `CLAUDE.md:66`).
+- `/sc:pr-submit` is carried out by Claude following the command and skill files. Expected results check the PR on GitHub, the git state and the run-log on disk, plus the exact strings those files fix; other chat wording is judged on content.
+
+## What you're verifying
+
+- The installed command defaults to level 3, caps `--max-rounds` at 5, has `--pr <N>`, and no longer lists `--yes`; the Python core enforces the same bounds and the head-binding check.
+- `--monitor 0` only opens the PR, on the `origin` repository `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude`, and starts no monitor.
+- A checkout that is not the PR head stops with `pr_head_mismatch`; `--max-rounds 6` is refused; `--yes` does nothing.
+- `--monitor 1 --pr <N>` proposes fixes and changes nothing; `--monitor 2 --pr <N>` edits only the working tree and stops before pushing; a bare `/sc:pr-submit --pr <N>` (level 3) commits one fix per cycle on top of the PR head, pushes it to the PR branch without force, replies to and resolves the fixed threads, and posts one re-review comment per present reviewer.
