+## Cleanup
+
+```bash
+gh pr close "$N" --repo IronbellyOrg/IronClaude --delete-branch --comment "D07 sandbox finished."
+gh pr view "$N" --repo IronbellyOrg/IronClaude --json state -q .state
+cd /tmp && rm -rf /tmp/d07
+```
+
+The first command is `[EXTERNAL]`: it closes the sandbox PR and deletes its remote branch; the second must print `CLOSED`. The last removes the clone, its virtual environment, the run-logs and the snapshot files. The closed PR, its comments and the review threads stay on GitHub. The Tier C sessions stay in Claude Code's own session history, and the hook state and log files they wrote under `~/.claude/state/` and `~/.claude/logs/` stay, like those of any session. No step changed your IronClaude install.
